  "note": "Lika River masonry bridge with three clear stone vaults, two round through-oculi, dressed voussoirs, low rounded pier plinths, plain coping and a narrow paved deck. The retained outline and attributed route establish the signed axis and bank contacts. Vault proportions, oculi and coping follow ordinary side photographs. The deck grade and approach support fit the standard terrain. The south approach terrain is lower than the deck in the source DEM. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
